A specimen record brings together identification, preparation, capture
data, and the physical parts of a specimen. Each specimen links to a
collecting event, which supplies the locality, method, collector, and
coordinate.

## In this section

- [Setting up specimen records](/en/usages/specimens/setup/): configure field IDs, tissue IDs, specimen types, and treatments before data entry.
- [Adding a new specimen record](/en/usages/specimens/add-record/): add a record with the `+` button {% ref id="A" /%}, then select the `Cataloger` {% ref id="B" /%}, `Taxon` {% ref id="D" /%}, and `Condition` {% ref id="C" /%}.
- [Collection and Identification](/en/usages/specimens/collection-and-identification/): core specimen metadata and the read-only taxonomy panel.
- [Capture Records](/en/usages/specimens/capture-records/): link the specimen to its collecting event, site, method, and coordinate.
- [Measurements](/en/usages/specimens/measurements/): the measurement form {% ref id="E" /%}, shared fields, and one page per taxon group, including bat fields {% ref id="F" /%} for mammals.
- [Specimen Parts](/en/usages/specimens/parts/): voucher preparations, tissues, and parasites {% ref id="G" /%}.
- [Associated Data and Media](/en/usages/specimens/associated-data-and-media/): linked digital data, files, and media.
- [Managing specimen records](/en/usages/specimens/managing-records/): duplicate, sort, export, import, and delete specimen records.
